Installed, but `blender-mcp.exe` is in `C:\Users\enakr\AppData\Roaming\Python\Python314\Scripts` which is NOT on PATH. So in the opencode config I should use the full path to the exe, to be safe.

Now create the project opencode.json with the MCP server config. The config:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "mcp": {
    "blender": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": ["C:\\Users\\enakr\\AppData\\Roaming\\Python\\Python314\\Scripts\\blender-mcp.exe"],
      "enabled": true
    }
  }
}
```

The blender-mcp server defaults to host 127.0.0.1 port 9876 for the Blender socket connection.

Also the user needs the Blender addon. The addon file is `addon.py` from the ahujasid/blender-mcp GitHub repo. I could download it for them to a known place, so they can install it in Blender GUI: Edit > Preferences > Add-ons > Install (the dropdown) > select addon.py > enable "Interface: Blender MCP".

Let me download the addon.py to the project folder (maybe D:\Projects\Others\Game\ModelsBlender\ or a Tools folder). URL: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ahujasid/blender-mcp/main/addon.py

Let me verify the exe exists first, then write config, then download addon.py.

Also I should remind about restarting opencode to load the MCP config.

